    'remediation.operator_e24252c37930e352' = 'Re-run the cycle once the root cause is resolved'
    'remediation.operator_e344b12d616e0f0a' = @(
        'elevation_required on '
        @{
            'arg' = 'vmName'
            'type' = 'detail'
            'trust' = 'external'
        }
        ': a command needed sudo and no operator was present to supply a password. sudo reads the password from /dev/tty, so this cannot be answered by the runner, by a retry, or from a remote session -- and a host in this state would otherwise stall mid-cycle while the dashboard still showed the last cycle green. Fixing it needs console access, exactly like a network fault does.'
    )
    'remediation.operator_e54de45d1485fbb7' = @(
        'ip_not_discovered on '
        @{
            'arg' = 'vmName'
            'type' = 'detail'
            'trust' = 'external'
        }
        ': no host-side probe could name an address for the guest, so the step never reached it. Address discovery rests on caches that age out and daemons that publish late, so the same call usually answers seconds later. Distinct from network_timeout, where an address WAS found and the path to it failed, and from host_network_degraded, which does not clear on its own.'
    )
    'remediation.operator_e54e017fda4a02ac' = @(
